## Mission Statement Methodology

The `mission-statement.json` must follow this structure:

```json
{
    "Name": "",
    "Purpose": "Statement of purpose that summarizes the business solution goals to be realized from (agents/solutionArchitect/in) and that can finish the statement 'The purpose of the product is to ...'",
    "Responsibilities": [
        "It is the responsibility of the SuD to contribute to g. Here g is any of the solution goals"
    ],
    "Exclusions": [
        "Reason why a particular functionality is excluded from the scope of the SuD"
    ]
}
```

### Guidelines

- "MUST" relate the goals of the SuD with **enviroment-goals**
- "MUST" relate the desired properties of the SuD to **business-goals** (must be on the in/ dir)


### Purpose Guidelines
- "MUST" make clear to what top-level **enviroment-goal** the system contributes
- "MUST" be the highest level goal to which the SuD contributes
- "MUST" follow the syntax "The purpose of the <Sud_Name> is to contribute to name **enviroment goals**"

### Responsibilities Guidelines
- "MUST" be a relationship between the SuD and some **desired-effect**
- "MUST" be a requirement that the the SuD contributes to the achievement of an **enviroment-goal** (must reasemble the in/requirements.md if any)
- "MUST" follow the syntax "It is a responsability of the <SuD name> to achieve **enviroment-goal**"
- each responsability "MUST" correspond to a list of **services**
- each responsability "MUST" be described in one or two more sentences
Organize system responsibilities according to:
- The Business goals they contribute to on (agents/solutionArchitect/in)
- The Business process in which they are used
- The external entities that are needed to exercise the responsibilities
- The kind of added value they deliver to the environment


### Exclusion Guidelines
- "MUST" be a responsability that the SuD is not going to have
- Each exclussion "MUST" be described in one or two more sentences
- "MUST" be organized according to
    - The business-goals they contribute to
    - The business process in which they are used
    - The external entities that are needed to excersice the responsabilities
    - The kind of added value they deliver to the enviroment



